PVD("tonga_vision_2015-2025",{"docs":["","TO Strategic Development Framework 2015 2025"],"s":{"1":[[1,"9","6","Anti-Corruption Commission Establishment","Government will put in place a sound governance framework including the establishment of an anti-corruption commission to protect the integrity of the government and gain the trust of the public.",""],[1,"9","6","Public Service Performance Improvement Measures","Government will strive to establish the conditions that ensure committed efforts from public servants to perform and to improve the Public Service, an essential aspect of ensuring that government operations are more productive and responsive to the needs of the country.",""],[1,"19","11","Law and Order Implementation and Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthened implementation and enforcement of law and order in a more inclusive, fair and transparent manner which helps resolve disputes, more effectively punishes and rehabilitates those who have broken the law, while supporting the population to go about their legitimate daily business without fear or favour from government.",""],[1,"20","1","Constitutional and Legal Framework Modernization","Modern and appropriate constitution, laws and regulations, reflecting international standards of democratic processes and procedures for political institutions, providing an efficient and effective legal structure that provides inclusive access, human rights and the protections required for a higher quality of life, as well as supporting the development of the appropriate institutions required for a progressive Tonga in a peaceful, constructive and effective manner.",""],[1,"70","3","Public Financial Management Reform","Major reform programs are underway related to improving governance including public financial management as part of the general management and performance of the public service.",""],[1,"70","3","Institutional Arrangements Reform Following Constitutional Changes","The recent major constitutional changes are still working through our institutional arrangements, including the way the Privy Council, executive, legislative and judicial parts of government interact, and the method by which we seek a strong rule of law, transparency and accountability within government and for all the people.",""],[1,"70","6","Public Service Performance and Anti-Corruption Reform","Such a service needs to be build on clear performance incentives and rejection of corruption.",""],[1,"71","3","Law and Order Implementation and Enforcement Strengthening","TSDF Organisational Outcome 3.2: Strengthened implementation and enforcement of law and order in a more inclusive, fair and transparent manner which helps resolve disputes, more effectively punishes and rehabilitates those who have broken the law, while supporting the population to go about their legitimate daily business without fear or favour from government.",""],[1,"71","6","Judicial Structure Development","This includes developing a judicial structure which is more accessible and consistent with standards of good practice in Commonwealth countries.",""],[1,"72","1","Constitutional and Legal Framework Modernization","Modern and appropriate constitution, laws and regulations, reflecting international standards of democratic processes and procedures for political institutions, providing an efficient and effective legal structure that provides inclusive access, human rights and the protections required for a higher quality of life, as well as supporting the development of the appropriate institutions required for a progressive Tonga in a peaceful, constructive and effective manner.",""],[1,"121","1","Leadership Code Enforcement","a) enforcement of the Leadership Code",""],[1,"121","4","Public Service Commission Reform Programme","continue implementation of Public Service Commission reform programs through improved regulations, appropriate remuneration, and improved staff performance management system",""],[1,"121","5","Public Financial Management Reform","continue public financial management reform with updated legislation, improved policy, national planning, integrated corporate planning and budgeting, procurement, financial management, revenue raising and auditing",""],[1,"121","8","Ministry of Justice Institutional Reform","improve the functioning of the Ministry of Justice based on reform of the Tongan Judicial system.","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"121","9","Anti-Corruption Office Strengthening Reform","strengthen the role of the Anti-Corruption Office with clear procedures and independent funding to challenge misapplication of the law and corruption",""],[1,"121","10","Strengthen Internal and External Government Audit","develop more internal auditing by government MDAs, supported by stronger external Audit",""],[1,"122","7","Judicial Structure and Judge Selection Reform","modify the judicial structure and process for appointing panellists to select judges to ensure greater transparency and accountability to the public, taking account of the advice from the Constitutional and Electoral Commission Report.",""]],"2":[[1,"100","15","Public Enterprise Sustainability, Accountability, and Privatization Reform","Ensuring Public Enterprises are sustainable and accountable, and where appropriate moved into the private sector.",""],[1,"117","5","Public Enterprise Supervision Strengthening","strengthen the appropriate supervisory conditions and criteria that encourage improved management and performance of PEs taking account of the various demands on them",""],[1,"117","6","Public Enterprise Management and Ownership Options Review","consider, as appropriate, various options for the management and ownership of PEs to improve performance in terms of profitability, accountability, and return on equity",""],[1,"117","7","Costing of Social Delivery Requirements and Subsidy Transparency for PE Operations","ensure social delivery requirements from PE are clearly costed and there are no hidden subsidies undermining the viability of its operations",""]],"3":[[1,"119","14","Affordable Universal Health Coverage Expansion","continue to work to provide affordable Universal Health Coverage with expanded coverage taking particular account of the specific needs of different groups, including women, men, children, the disabled etc.",""],[1,"119","16","National Health Service Capacity Strengthening","strengthened national capacity to deliver high-quality health services including family planning and services to prevent HIV and STIs, for young people, sensitive to the different needs of women and men",""],[1,"119","17","National Referral and Regional Health Services Network Strengthening","maintaining and improving the network of health services delivered through the national referral hospital at Vaiola, supported by a network of regional hospitals and community clinics, to deliver effective health care",""],[1,"119","18","ICT-Enabled Cost-Effective Service Delivery","seeking new and innovative options, including ICT, for cost effective service delivery.",""]],"4":[[1,"74","6","Island Transport Services Improvement","More reliable, safe and affordable transport services on each island, connecting islands and connecting the Kingdom with the rest of the world by sea and air, to improve the movement of people and goods.",""],[1,"123","9","Transport Infrastructure Construction, Management and Maintenance","provide improved transport infrastructure construction, management and maintenance",""],[1,"123","10","Island Road Network Improvement","improve road networks on islands",""],[1,"123","11","Minimum Transport Infrastructure Policy for Island Connectivity","development a minimum transport infrastructure policy providing the minimum standard for connecting each island to the national transport network",""],[1,"123","12","International Shipping and Aviation Safety Compliance","ensure adherence with international shipping and aviation safety regulations and standards",""],[1,"123","13","Private Sector Transport Services Support","support strong private sector aviation, shipping services and land transport services in country",""],[1,"123","14","International Shipping and Aviation Connectivity Promotion","encourage more international shipping and aviation links to the country",""],[1,"123","15","Transport Regulatory Standards Enforcement","maintain and enforce appropriate air, sea and land transport regulatory standards and requirements",""]],"5":[[1,"10","1","Strengthened Monitoring and Evaluation System","Progress requires improved and honest monitoring and evaluation of what we do and what we deliver.",""],[1,"13","1","Integrated Planning and Budgeting System Reform","The language and structure builds on the ongoing reform process to build a more integrated planning and budgeting system.",""],[1,"14","1","National Outcomes and Organisational Outcomes Framework","The Outcome Objectives and Enabling Themes of TSDFI have been merged into a more tightly articulated set of National Outcomes which are supported by clear Organisational Outcomes (see Annex 4: Plotting TSDFI to TSDFII and Annex 5: Plotting TSDFII to TSDFI).",""],[1,"14","1","MDA Corporate Plan Alignment and Output Articulation","These Organisational Outcomes provide clear guidance to government Ministries, Departments and Agencies (MDAs), and other organisations, on the Organisational Outputs they need to deliver.",""],[1,"21","6","Strengthened Monitoring and Evaluation System","Government intends to establish a stronger, more focussed system for monitoring and evaluation (M&E) of progress during TSDFII.","National Planning & Economic Development Division of MFNP"],[1,"21","6","Enhanced National Data Compilation and Dissemination for M&E","Staff will work closely with the National Bureau of Statistics, the National Reserve Bank of Tonga (NRBT) and other key agencies to improve the compilation and distribution of more accurate, timely and informative data and analysis for better M&E.","National Bureau of Statistics | National Reserve Bank of Tonga (NRBT) | MFNP"],[1,"24","6","Integrated Planning and Budgeting System Development","Chapter 5 explains the role of the TSDF at the top of the cascading integrated planning and budgeting system we are developing.",""],[1,"24","6","Organizational Outcomes and Outputs Delegation Framework","The delegation of Organizational Outcomes and responsibility for developing Organizational Outputs, in particular by government Ministries, Departments and Agencies (MDAs) is explained.",""],[1,"24","6","Monitoring, Evaluation and Reporting System Strengthening","The essential role of a strong monitoring, evaluation and reporting system to track progress is outlined.",""],[1,"24","6","TSDF II Constraint-Addressing Reform","TSDF II seeks to address these constraints.",""],[1,"25","2","Administrative Data Quality Improvement Reform","Part of the ongoing administrative reforms included within the TSDF cover improving the quality and accuracy of data available to help with monitoring progress and designing new and appropriate plans, policies and projects.",""],[1,"42","12","Integrated Government Planning and Budgeting Reform","A major program of reform of central functions of government is also ongoing.",""],[1,"43","2","Improved Data for Results Chain Monitoring and Reporting","Each of the levels in the results chain must be supported by improved data for better analysis, monitoring, evaluation and reporting of performance.",""],[1,"43","2","Integration of Data Improvements with Public Financial Management and Staff Performance Systems","This work is also linked into related public financial management reforms and staff performance management systems.",""],[1,"43","2","Disaggregated Data Collection and Analysis Improvement","The collection, compilation, analysis and distribution of accurate, informative and timely data is a major weaknesses.",""],[1,"46","2","Resilience Monitoring Improvement","We shall have to improve our monitoring of such changes to improve our resilience.",""],[1,"46","3","Integrated Planning and Budgeting Framework Strengthening","A stronger more result based framework, that we are building for our integrated planning and budgeting system is also recognized as appropriate for the TSDF.",""],[1,"46","3","Planning and Monitoring Data Improvement","More accurate, timely, disaggregated data is also essential for both the planning phase and for monitoring performance and progress.",""],[1,"46","3","Skills and Capacity Building for Modern Planning Tools","With this we need to be able to build the required skills and capacity, supported by the necessary attitudes and behaviours, required to use these modern tools.",""],[1,"47","11","Results Framework Alignment with Integrated Planning and Budgeting Reforms","Aligning behind a Results Framework consistent with the integrated planning and budgeting reforms: Each level of the TSDF results chain is more carefully articulated.",""],[1,"79","10","Integrated Consultation, Monitoring, Evaluation and Reporting System","Consultation, monitoring, evaluation (M&E) and reporting are built into each level.",""],[1,"79","10","Staff Performance Management System Improvement","This includes improved staff performance management systems.",""],[1,"79","12","Priority Agenda Establishment","Some governments may wish to also establish a Priority Agenda, which highlights particular aspects of the TSDF and other level plans to receive priority focus during their term in office.",""],[1,"79","12","Annual Budget Strategy and Funding Envelope Guidance","This will provide additional guidance and focus to the annual Budget Strategy and Funding Envelopes for the three year Medium Term Budget Framework (MTBF) which provides the guidance for local and aid funding.",""],[1,"79","12","Corporate Plan Revision Alignment","The Strategy and Envelope also guide the revision to the Corporate Plans to help ensure these plans and budgets are in balance.",""],[1,"79","13","Medium-Term Macroeconomic Framework Improvement","Further improvements to the medium term macroeconomic framework, within which the MTBF can be situated, will help to improve the forecasting and management of resources (both domestic and aid) for the implementation of the lower level plans guided by the TSDF.",""],[1,"79","13","Resource Linking Through Budget and Fiscal Strategy Documents","The MTFB, and associated budget documents, also include the more detailed fiscal strategies that guide the linking of resources with the shorter term priorities drawn from the TSDF, and emphasised in any Priority Agenda and other plans.",""],[1,"80","4","Close Institutional Gaps in Planning and Budgeting","Closing these gaps will be an essential step to improve planning and budgeting and their implementation.",""],[1,"82","5","Evidence-Based Planning and Budgeting Reform","use knowledge-based analysis, appraisal, planning, and budgeting based on improved, more disaggregated, data and evidence - to better inform our decisions",""],[1,"82","7","Policy, Plan, Program, Project, Budget, and Guidance Development","develop better articulated policies, plans, programs, projects. budgets and guidance - to help us be clearer about the details of where we want to go and how",""],[1,"82","8","Capacity Strengthening for Improved Delivery","continue to strengthen capacity for improved delivery building on appropriate institutions, behaviours, attitudes, technology and infrastructure - to ensure we can do what we plan",""],[1,"82","9","Monitoring, Evaluation and Reporting Improvement","develop better monitoring, evaluation (M&E) and reporting, based on the same data improvements as required in step 1 - to ensure that we actually are going in the direction we want and avoiding too many unintended consequences.",""],[1,"86","9","Strengthened National Monitoring and Evaluation System","Government intends to establish a stronger, more focussed system for monitoring and evaluation (M&E) of the progress during TSDFII.","National Planning & Economic Development Division of MFNP"],[1,"86","10","Expanded Multi-Stakeholder Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","The Unit will give further consideration on how to build the M&E within a wider range of institutions from CSO and business.",""],[1,"86","10","Public-Private Partnership Approach for Responsible M&E","The objective will be to build on good practice in joint public/private partnerships for more responsible and accountable M&E.",""],[1,"86","10","National Development Oversight Committee Structure","The design of such an oversight committee structure will include focus on becoming more responsive and adaptive to unexpected changes to increase the country's resilience.",""],[1,"87","2","Strengthening M&E Data Compilation and Dissemination","Staff from the M&E Unit will work closely with the National Bureau of Statistics, the National Reserve Bank of Tonga (NRBT) and other key MDAs to improve the compilation and distribution of more accurate, timely and informative data and analysis for better M&E.","National Bureau of Statistics | National Reserve Bank of Tonga (NRBT) | other key MDAs"],[1,"121","6","Improved Monitoring and Evaluation System","better monitoring and evaluation based on improved data (broken into key categories, including gender and age) for tracking performance",""],[1,"127","8","Sector Plan Approval and Implementation Start","all 6 sector growth committees to have their \"Sector Plans\" approved; implementation work started",""]],"6":[[1,"10","1","Ongoing Development Partnership Engagement","We seek their ongoing partnership to help our development, to improve our competitive advantage, to enrich our culture and to protect our society, especially in the face of increasing challenges from the world around us.",""],[1,"20","3","Development Partner Collaboration and Dialogue Mechanism","Improved collaboration and dialogue with our development partners to ensure that their support is consistent with our needs and in line with the international standards set out in various international Declarations and Accords.",""],[1,"22","23","Development Partner Coordination and Alignment Mechanism","Improved collaboration with development partners ensuring programs better aligned behind gov't priorities",""],[1,"23","22","Development Partner Coordination and Alignment Mechanism","Improved collaboration with development partners ensuring programs better aligned behind gov't priorities",""],[1,"60","30","Development Partner Coordination for Program Alignment","Improved collaboration with development partners ensuring programs better aligned behind gov't priorities",""],[1,"72","4","External Aid Coordination and Harmonization Mechanism","Improved coordination, alignment and harmonization of external aid and development support, along with an equitable application across the country is critical for improving the contribution our partners make to our vision.",""],[1,"81","22","Development Partner Coordination and Alignment Mechanism","Improved collaboration with development partners ensuring programs better aligned behind gov't priorities",""],[1,"82","6","Participatory Consultative Planning Approach","use participatory consultative approaches with relevant stakeholders, both inside and outside of government - to improve participation, inclusion and coordination",""],[1,"122","10","Aid Effectiveness Initiative for Small Island States","actively engage in initiatives to improve the effectiveness of aid and development assistance to small island states",""],[1,"122","11","Development Partner Relations and Donor Harmonisation","continue to maintain good relations with development partners, for mutual partnership, aid effectiveness and donor harmonisation",""],[1,"122","13","Government Development Partner Coordination Improvement","improve coordination within government on the management of relations and assistance from our various development partners.",""]],"7":[[1,"73","1","Peacekeeping-Linked Skills Development for HMAF","regional and international peace-keeping arrangements allows us to link into extensive external support that helps to build skills in HMAF which also supports disaster management in Tonga and expands the skills base of current and former soldiers.",""],[1,"73","7","Scientific Problem-Solving and Innovation Adoption","The more expansive our world view, the more willing we will be experiment and apply the scientific method to problem solving.",""],[1,"73","7","Inclusive Skills and Behaviour Development","This is only possible, however, if we chose values that allow us to develop the skills, attitudes and behaviour in a more inclusive manner.",""],[1,"100","7","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Improvement","Appropriately skilled workforce to meet the available opportunities in Tonga and overseas, by delivering improved Technical and Vocational Education and Training.",""],[1,"101","13","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Improvement","by delivering improved Technical and Vocational Education and Training.",""],[1,"102","7","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Improvement","Appropriately skilled workforce to meet the available opportunities in Tonga and overseas, by delivering improved Technical and Vocational Education and Training.",""],[1,"102","14","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Improvement","Appropriately skilled workforce to meet the available opportunities in Tonga and overseas, by delivering improved Technical and Vocational Education and Training.",""],[1,"119","9","Skills Development through Domestic and External Training Opportunities","promoting skills development through appropriate development of domestic training institutions, and mobilization of external training opportunities",""],[1,"119","10","Workforce Skills Strengthening Programme","strengthen the skills of the workforce to increase production, exports and overseas employment of Tongans, both men and women",""],[1,"119","13","Expanded Training Opportunities for HMAF Members","make greater use of the training options available to members of HMAF.",""],[1,"123","8","Local Energy Expert Capacity-Building Initiative","enhance the capabilities of local energy experts to build their expertise through appropriately involving local energy consultancies and professional works.",""],[1,"124","3","ICT Skills Training Expansion","expand training and skills in the use of modern ICT, including encouraging foreign investment in this area",""],[1,"124","11","Scientific and Technical Training Improvement","improve scientific and technical training at secondary and tertiary level to increase the number of students with appropriate skills",""]],"8":[[1,"109","12","Alternative Technology Service Delivery for Health and Education","opportunities to deliver services (e.g. health and education) using alternative technologies rather than building clinics and schools",""],[1,"118","15","Virtual Museum Development","develop a virtual museum so that Tongans, especially schoolchildren, can view items of historical and cultural significance from Tonga and elsewhere",""],[1,"119","3","Government Provision of Early Childhood and Primary Education","continuing to focus on government provision of early childhood education (ECE) and primary education for all",""],[1,"119","4","Partnerships for Secondary and Tertiary Education Provision","continue working in partnership with the churches and other groups for the provision of secondary education and tertiary education",""],[1,"119","5","Education Sector Strategy Implementation for Universal Basic Education","supporting and improving universal basic education through the implementation of the education sector strategy",""],[1,"119","6","Gender-Balanced Education System Development","develop an education system that better addresses the needs of both girls and boys and ensures a better gender balance at all stages of schooling",""],[1,"119","7","ICT-Enabled Education Service Delivery Improvement","identify more effective opportunities, including new ICT, to help deliver education services across the Kingdom in a more effective and affordable manner",""],[1,"119","8","Curriculum and Education Standards Regulation","government to continue to set the curriculum and standards for education delivery, while encouraging greater non-government provision of the services",""],[1,"119","11","Knowledge-Based Research and Development Capacity Promotion","i) promote knowledge based research and development (R&D) capacity addressing the needs in Tonga",""],[1,"119","12","Education Service Delivery Efficiency Improvement","seek more cost-effective means of delivering a higher quality education service throughout the country",""],[1,"120","6","Implementation of Disability-Inclusive Development and Inclusive Education Policies","ensure effective implementation of related policies such as National Policy on Disability Inclusive Development, and Inclusive Education Policy which ensures children with disabilities get appropriate education; effective implantation of the National Policy on Mental Health",""]],"9":[[1,"109","12","Renewable Energy and Energy Efficiency Financing Support","improving financial support for renewable and energy efficiency development",""],[1,"123","5","Cost-Effective Petroleum Products Delivery and Distribution Options","seek options for more cost-effective delivery, storage and distribution of petroleum products",""],[1,"123","6","Alternative Energy Production and Distribution Systems Development","further develop technically reliable, economically affordable and environmentally sound alternative energy production and distribution systems to support the sustainable development of the Kingdom",""],[1,"123","7","Energy Saving Awareness and Application Programme","continue to develop awareness and application of energy saving opportunities to help constrain the growth in energy demand",""]],"10":[[1,"120","4","Waste Management Improvement and Communicable Disease Prevention","work with others to improve waste management and limit conditions which facilitate communicable diseases.",""],[1,"125","8","Safe Water Supply Management and Delivery Improvement","improve the management and delivery of safe water supply for business and households",""],[1,"125","14","Public Awareness on Pollution and Waste Management Impacts","increase understanding by business and households of the health and economic damage from pollution and poor waste management, and the benefits to livelihoods and wellbeing from a cleaner environment in particular as it impacts different groups",""],[1,"126","1","Environmental Capacity-Building and Enforcement Framework","build the capacity, both in government and the community, to better ensure clean and healthy environments with an appropriate mix of enforcement and encouragement",""],[1,"126","2","Private Sector Participation in Pollution Control and Waste Management Services","increase private sector participation in the provision of services for pollution control and waste management, and where this is lacking complement it with appropriate levels of services provide by government through public enterprises",""],[1,"126","3","Community Environmental Awareness and Outreach Program","engage all level of stakeholders (including focus on women, men, youth, schools and other groups) in communal awareness and outreach programs to enhance their level of understanding and participation in living in a cleaner and sustainable environment",""],[1,"126","4","National Solid Waste Reduction and Recycling Program","develop an effective country-wide program to proactively reduce the creation of solid waste (including e-waste) and manage the segregation, disposal and recycling of wastes.",""]],"11":[[1,"125","9","Biodiversity Conservation Planning and Management Tools","develop appropriate planning frameworks and management tools for the conservation of biodiversity and sustainable use of the environment, while maintaining ecosystem services",""],[1,"125","10","Sustainable Resource Use Policy Development","develop better policies for guiding the use of these resources in a sustainable manner",""],[1,"125","11","Environmental and Resource Planning Streamlining","streamline environmental and resources planning and evidence-based decision making processes, using disaggregated data and plans, to address the particular account of the needs of special groups (women, disabled, etc.)",""],[1,"125","12","Science and Technical Capacity Strengthening for Government Agencies","improve science and technical knowledge base within key government agencies to better manage our resources",""],[1,"125","13","Seabed Mining Governance Framework","put in place policies, legislation and systems for managing the physical and fiscal consequences of seabed mining to mitigate the 'resource curse' and ensure the benefits contribute to our vision not our destruction.",""]],"12":[[1,"59","3","Environmental Assessments and Disaster Management Response for Vulnerable Communities","To protect the quality of life, special attention to their needs will be built into environmental assessments and disaster management response.",""],[1,"100","9","Integration of Sustainability and Risk Management into Programme Planning","Cultural awareness, environmental sustainability, disaster risk management and climate change adaptation, integrated into all planning and implementation of programmes, by establishing and adhering to appropriate procedures and consultation mechanisms.",""],[1,"101","18","Mainstreaming of Cultural Awareness, Environmental Sustainability, Disaster Risk Management, and Climate Adaptation","Cultural awareness, environmental sustainability, disaster risk management and climate change adaptation, integrated into all planning and implementation of programmes, by establishing and adhering to appropriate procedures and consultation mechanisms.",""],[1,"102","16","Integration of Sustainability and Disaster Risk Procedures into Programme Planning","Cultural awareness, environmental sustainability, disaster risk management and climate change adaptation, integrated into all planning and implementation of programmes, by establishing and adhering to appropriate procedures and consultation mechanisms.",""],[1,"102","24","Mainstreaming Cultural Awareness, Environmental Sustainability, Disaster Risk Management, and Climate Adaptation","Cultural awareness, environmental sustainability, disaster risk management and climate change adaptation, integrated into all planning and implementation of programmes, by establishing and adhering to appropriate procedures and consultation mechanisms.",""],[1,"117","9","Disaster Risk Management Integration into PE Plans and Investments","disaster risk management to be integrated into all PE plans and investments to mitigate effects of disasters.",""],[1,"121","13","Police-HMAF Emergency Collaboration Mechanism","f) further develop the collaboration between Police and HMAF during national emergencies",""],[1,"121","14","Tonga Fire Service Coverage Expansion","increase the coverage of the Tonga Fire Service, complementing other disaster mitigation capacities of government.",""],[1,"126","5","Climate and Disaster Data and Technical Knowledge Improvement","improve the technical knowledge and local data base of severe natural events and the impact of climate change to better inform policy making and monitor implementation",""],[1,"126","6","Climate and Disaster Risk Mainstreaming Guidelines","ensure appropriate enabling policy and guidelines to ensure the incorporation of relevant climate change and disaster risk management considerations into the design and implementation of all relevant policies, plans, projects and budgets",""],[1,"126","7","Community Disaster Preparedness, Response and Recovery Protocols","improve protocols for disaster preparedness, response and recovery of communities after natural disaster",""],[1,"126","9","Environmental and Resources Management Capacity Strengthening","strengthen analytical and assessment capabilities of environmental and resources management MDAs to enhance community preparedness and resilience to impacts of all disasters",""],[1,"126","10","Institutional Capacity Development for Climate Risk Management in Agriculture","develop institutional capacity to support climate risk management in agricultural crops and land management for food and nutritional security",""],[1,"126","11","Multi-Hazard Early Warning Systems Improvement","improve multi-hazard early warning systems to enhance disaster preparedness",""],[1,"126","12","Weather, Climate and Environment Monitoring and Service Delivery Improvement","improve weather, climate and environment monitoring, research and service delivery through better informed vulnerability, mitigation strategies and adaptation measures.",""],[1,"126","13","Disaster Management Infrastructure Improvement","improve disaster management infrastructures through better support emergency management.",""]],"13":[[1,"9","7","Government-Business-Civil Society Partnership for Development","Working together, government, business, civil society and the people will reform and progress and pass on an enhanced inheritance to our children:",""],[1,"62","5","Public-Private Partnership for Business Environment Reform","Government works closely to develop collaborative partnerships with the private sector to help identify and address constraints to the development of a more dynamic business environment and level of economic activity.",""],[1,"63","4","Public-Private Partnership and Business Linkage Promotion","Close cooperation and partnership, especially in a small economy, is important to ensure government and the private sector are working together effectively to address the constraints to growth.",""],[1,"63","4","Joint Venture Management and Public Enterprise Funding Options","Such partnerships also include options for joint venture management and funding options for public enterprises.",""],[1,"63","6","Business Regulation and Investment Incentive Framework","Government has the responsibility to set the rules and regulations under which people engage in trade and business.",""],[1,"90","3","Community Development Partnership Framework","Closer partnership between government, churches & other stakeholders for community development",""],[1,"100","4","Public-Private Partnership Promotion and Regulatory Streamlining","Dynamic public and private sector partnership as the engine of growth, by promoting better collaboration between government and business, appropriate incentives and streamlining of rules and regulations.",""],[1,"101","7","Public-Private Partnership Promotion and Regulatory Streamlining","Dynamic public and private sector partnership as the engine of growth, by promoting better collaboration between government and business, appropriate incentives and streamlining of rules and regulations.",""],[1,"102","6","Public-Private Partnership Promotion and Regulatory Streamlining","Dynamic public and private sector partnership as the engine of growth, by promoting better collaboration between goverment and business, appropriate incentives and streamlining of rules and regulations.",""],[1,"116","8","Stakeholder Consultative Mechanisms for MDAs","ensure all MDAs of government have effective consultative mechanisms for engaging with stakeholders to help address constraints to growth, including the six Sector Growth Committees covering agriculture, fisheries, tourism, construction, manufacturing and commerce",""],[1,"116","10","Infrastructure Investment Financing and Risk Guarantee Mechanism","establish infrastructure investment financing and risk guarantee mechanisms to facilitate private sector interest in all sectors",""],[1,"116","11","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Large Business and Infrastructure Management","seek opportunities for joint public/private partnerships for management and funding of larger businesses, including infrastructure",""],[1,"117","8","Public Enterprise Consumer Consultation Mechanism","ensure all Public Enterprises have effective consultative mechanism for listening to the needs of consumers",""],[1,"117","13","Investment Promotion Regulatory Framework","provide clear and transparent rules, regulations, incentives and information which encourages both foreign and domestic investment",""]],"14":[[1,"73","7","Technology and Infrastructure Solutions for Institutional Development","The more willing we are to apply new technological and infrastructure solutions, the greater the range of institutional arrangements we can develop.",""],[1,"117","4","Digital Business Licensing and Regulatory Improvement","use modern technology, as appropriate to improve business licensing and other regulations to increase access and timeliness of response, taking particular note of the special needs of business on outer islands and the transport and communications difficulties they face.",""],[1,"121","7","ICT-Based Information Management and E-Government Expansion","better use of information and communication technology (ICT) for the management of information, and extension of e-government.",""],[1,"124","1","National Telecommunications Network Expansion","extend the cable connection from Tongatapu to the other main centres supported by improved microwave links",""],[1,"124","2","ICT Applications Expansion for Digital Services","expand the applications of ICT to include e-government, e-commerce, e-learning, e-disaster and e-entertainment",""],[1,"125","2","Land Administration and E-Based Land Records Information System","further strengthen the land administration framework, recording and management of land records, building into governments plans for an e-based information system",""]],"15":[[1,"9","7","Multi-stakeholder Reform and Development Participation","All citizens should take part in the reforms and play their role in the development process.",""],[1,"9","7","Whole-of-Society Governance Reform Framework","Efficiency, effectiveness, transparency, honesty and living within our inheritance are essential to the success of this Framework.",""],[1,"20","2","Inter-Branch Coordination Improvement","Improved working relations and coordination between the Privy Council, Executive, Legislative & Judicial wings of government so that they work effectively together in support of the Tongan vision.",""],[1,"38","4","Institutional Arrangements Strengthening","Further work remains to be done during the TSDFII to fully embed these recent changes and ensure all institutional arrangements are working effectively.",""],[1,"38","4","Inter-Branch Government Coordination Framework","This includes the institutional arrangements between the Privy Council and the other arms of government: executive, legislature and judiciary.",""],[1,"38","4","Public Service Role Clarification and Professionalization","The relationship between these various arm and a apolitical and professional public service also need to be developed further.",""],[1,"53","3","Open and Inclusive Policy Deliberation Framework","This requires more open and inclusive debate.",""],[1,"53","3","Policy Experimentation and Adaptive Reform Mechanism","Where we do not have the definite answer we will try and test different options to find those which work more effectively.",""],[1,"53","3","Responsible Institutional Reform Framework","We will develop this within a responsible framework where we can build on successes, and be ready to modify arrangements were there is potential failure.",""],[1,"71","4","Town and District Officer Service Network","The government administration in Tonga is supported by a network of Town and District Officers across the Kingdom.",""],[1,"71","4","Constituency Office Development for Members of Parliament","The development of offices for Members of Parliament in their constituencies is further helping to improve the outreach of government to be more responsive to local needs.",""],[1,"71","4","Strengthening Inclusive Access to Government Services","More still needs to be done to strengthen this and to ensure more inclusive access across the Kingdom.",""],[1,"72","3","Inter-Branch Government Coordination Improvement","Improved working relations and coordination between the Privy Council, Executive, Legislative &Judicial wings of government so that they work effectively together in support of the Tongan vision.",""],[1,"80","3","Cross-Cutting Coordination Committees and Plans","Table 9 lists the crossing cutting plans and committees by organisations to show how these work together to support the TSDF.",""],[1,"101","26","Government Efficiency and Coordination Improvement","Continuing progress to a more efficient and effective government by focussing on its core functions; improving coordination, service delivery and optimising use of resources.",""],[1,"102","20","Government Efficiency and Coordination Improvement","Continuing progress to a more efficient and effective government by focussing on its core functions; improving coordination, service delivery and optimising use of resources.",""],[1,"121","2","Cross-Government Responsibility Delegation and Coordination Committees","clear delegation of responsibility across government MDAs, with an appropriate set of cross-cutting committees and working groups supporting a more integrated and collaborative governance",""],[1,"121","3","Policy Analysis and Implementation Capacity Strengthening","strengthening policy analysis and implementation capacity of government, based on improved data and evidence - ensuring data and analysis is broken down by different categories (such as gender) to ensure the needs of all groups are appropriately addressed",""],[1,"122","12","Administrative Systems Strengthening for Support Management","continue to build administrative systems to better manage this support while always seeking to use government systems as much as possible",""]],"16":[[1,"33","4","Formal Social Services for Vulnerable Families","For the first time in the history formal social services are now available in Tonga to help the most vulnerable elderly and the disabled.",""],[1,"33","4","Public-Private Partnership for Social Service Delivery","We have a Public Private Partnership with Government funding an NGO to provide social services to vulnerable families.",""],[1,"33","4","Inclusive Decision-Making Arrangements for Vulnerable People","New institutional arrangements are also giving vulnerable people greater input to decision making.",""],[1,"33","4","Expanded Elderly Benefit Support","Nearly 4000 people over the age of 70 have access to the increase in benefits to the elderly.",""],[1,"33","4","Rollout of Social Services for Vulnerable Elderly","About 600 of these will be eligible for the new social services being rolled out for the vulnerable elderly.",""],[1,"33","4","Social Services for Vulnerable Infants","At the other end of the age range, some 250 infants will be eligible for similar services.",""],[1,"90","10","Monitoring Systems for Vulnerable Groups","Monitoring systems for identifying and measuring problems faced by vulnerable groups are in place and being used by Government to target resources",""],[1,"120","5","Institutional Care and Support Services Expansion","increasing institutional care and support services for the elderly, disabled and other vulnerable groups, including investigation of the potential private sector role, which complements and supports traditional support structures rather than undermining them",""],[1,"120","7","Strengthen Social Protection, Disaster Management, and Poverty Alleviation Programs","strengthen social protection, disaster management and poverty alleviation programs for communities",""],[1,"120","9","Retirement Scheme Expansion and Management Reform","extend the retirement schemes to cover a wider share of the working population and ensure that these schemes are well managed",""]],"17":[[1,"37","1","Diaspora Engagement and Support Initiative","This relationship between Tongans in the Kingdom and those in the diaspora is a major asset that will be further supported and encouraged in TSDF II.",""],[1,"37","2","Immigrant and Overseas Tongan Integration Support","More will have to be done to help integrate and encourage both new immigrants and overseas Tongan to support the Vision of TSDF II.",""],[1,"117","14","Diaspora Exchange and Women’s Group Partnership Support","build on the opportunities of mutually beneficial exchange with our Diaspora around the world, with particular support for the exchange relations between women groups.",""],[1,"118","6","Returnee Reintegration Support","improve the integration of 'returnees' (those sent back to Tonga for violating overseas laws) so that they may become more constructive members of society and limit the transfer of undesirable behaviours",""],[1,"118","7","Integration Support for New Tongans","facilitate the integration of new Tongans into Tongan society.",""],[1,"120","11","Diaspora Engagement Institutional Arrangements and International Agreements","improve understanding of the many ways in which people resident in Tonga and overseas (in particular the Diaspora) interact in beneficial ways, and support the development of institutional arrangements and international agreements which facilitate this interaction - taking account of gender and other differences",""]],"18":[[1,"61","4","Special Arrangements for Formalization of Small Businesses","Special arrangements being implemented, including improved services on outer islands, make it easier for small businesses to move from the informal to the formal sector.",""],[1,"62","2","Support for Small Businesses and Outer Island Enterprises","Efforts to address the special needs of small businesses and those on outer islands are being made to ensure that all of the support to business development is not focused on business in Nuku'alofa.",""],[1,"62","7","Improved Service Delivery to Informal Sector and Remote Groups","supporting government outputs place greater focus on ensuring that their services are better delivered to the informal sector, outer islands and other difficult to access groups.",""],[1,"62","7","Promotion of Better Business Practices","It also requires them to promote better business practices",""],[1,"63","4","Inclusive Business Participation Mechanism","This engagement needs to ensure as wide a participation as possible to avoid it being dominated by larger formal businesses.",""],[1,"63","4","Formal-Informal Business Partnership Promotion","Encouraging business partnerships between larger formal sector business and smaller informal business can help to build links and greater symbiotic relationship between businesses.",""],[1,"116","3","Financial Services Sector Development and Inclusion","development of well regulated, responsible and competitive financial services (banking, insurance, microfinance etc.) which increase the of services available at more competitive interest rates, while giving particular attention to increased access for women and other groups who are less able to engage with the formal financial system",""],[1,"116","9","Targeted Outreach to Weaker and Less Connected Groups","make particular effort to ensure effective outreach to weaker and less connected groups (including outer islands, women groups, poorer groups)",""],[1,"117","2","Transparent and Inclusive Business Support Regulation","that all regulations and assistance to business are implemented in a transparent, honest and inclusive manner avoiding favour to special interest groups, and taking note of disadvantaged and vulnerable groups, with particular focus on needs of women entrepreneurs",""],[1,"117","3","Support for Small and Informal Business Formalization","make special consideration of the needs of small and informal businesses to encourage their greater engagement within the formal sector taking particular account of the constraints facing women entrepreneurs",""]],"19":[[1,"62","5","International Market Access Negotiation for Tongan Businesses and Workers","Government also leads in negotiating with other countries to expand the range of opportunities overseas for Tongan businesses and workers.",""],[1,"117","10","Trade Negotiation Capacity Building","ensure the capacity to engage effectively in regional and wider trade and access negotiations that support greater opportunities for Tongan exports and imports",""],[1,"117","11","Overseas Market Access Negotiation and Protocol Improvement","improve protocols and negotiate for greater access to overseas markets; in particular for agricultural and fisheries products",""],[1,"117","12","Overseas Employment Access Negotiation Initiative","negotiate for greater access to overseas employment schemes, in particular for more skilled workers and opportunities for women workers",""]],"20":[[1,"120","1","NCD Prevention Collaboration and Awareness Strengthening","strengthening the collaboration between Tonga Health systems and partners to promote and strengthened primary and secondary prevention of NCD risk factors and NCD-related diseases through whole of government and whole of society approaches building awareness and understanding of the courses and options for mitigating NCDs",""],[1,"120","2","Preventive Health Care Programme Improvement","improving efficiency and effectiveness of preventative health care programmes that encourage healthy life styles, including consumption of appropriate foods and increased exercise, so as to decrease the incidence of NCDs",""],[1,"120","3","NCD Complications Treatment Improvement","improve treatment of conditions arising from the complications associated with NCDs",""]],"21":[[1,"67","5","Legal and Funding Support for Social and Cultural Change","Government can, however, through the laws enacted, and the funding provided, encourage the choice of appropriate traditional and development values that support the evolution of our attitudes and behaviours which are more suitable to drive our vision.",""],[1,"67","5","Prevention of Violence Against Women and Children","This includes addressing unacceptable behaviour such as violence towards women, children and others.",""],[1,"67","5","Inclusive Public Consultation on Social and Cultural Change","This is an area where inclusive and participatory discussion and consultation is essential as it touches on the very foundation of our self-awareness as a people.",""],[1,"70","5","Inclusive Access to Government Services and Political Participation","To ensure more inclusive access to decision making, law and order and general government services TSDFII Pillar 3 Organisational Outcomes require supporting government outputs to place greater focus on ensuring that their services are better delivered to the all groups and that all groups have a better voice and participation in the political system.",""],[1,"118","5","Gender Development Policy Implementation","improve gender equality by implementing the government's gender development policy and ensuring a more balanced and effective engagement by both men and women in decision making and social, economic and political institutions",""],[1,"119","1","Gender Mainstreaming Across Policies and Initiatives","ensure that improved gender balance is built into all policies, plans, laws and initiatives",""],[1,"120","10","Gender and Inclusion Mainstreaming Across All Programs","build strong gender awareness, sensitivity to differences in needs in abilities, and other criteria into all programs",""],[1,"122","4","Inclusive Political Dialogue and Constitutional Reform Process","apply sound and inclusive systems, that provide a voice for all groups, including both women and men for debating the changing political conditions Tonga faces and how to address any further Constitutional and legal reforms agreed as desirable",""],[1,"122","5","Open and Inclusive Constitutional and Legal Amendment Process","ensure that all amendments to the Constitution and laws are managed in an open and inclusive process that gives people time to become informed of the changes and to provide their comments",""]],"22":[[1,"66","5","Improved Public Service Delivery for Outer Islands and Special Needs Groups","TSDFII Pillar 2 Organisational Outcomes require supporting government outputs to place greater focus on ensuring that their services are better delivered to all sectors of society, in particular outer islands and groups with special needs.",""],[1,"90","3","Community Development Partnership Framework","Closer partnership between government, churches & other stakeholders for community development",""],[1,"90","15","Community Sports and Cultural Participation Promotion","Increase in the number and promote active participation of the community groups and villages in any of the sports and cultural activities within Tonga and with the Tongan diaspora",""],[1,"118","1","Village Governance and Community Ownership Strengthening","strengthen village governance, build greater cohesion and facilitate community ownership of development initiatives",""],[1,"118","2","CSO and NGO Registration Support","encourage and support the registration of CSOs and NGOs working to support skills and services for communities throughout the Kingdom",""],[1,"118","4","Local Sports Participation Support","encourage participation by local sports groups in local and international sporting events, in particular the 2019 Pacific Games",""],[1,"118","10","Stakeholder Dialogue for Inclusive Service Coverage","facilitate constructive dialogue between the stakeholders to ensure that services effectively cover the whole country and all groups, in particular those with special needs",""],[1,"122","1","Outer Island and Rural Development Programme Improvement","better formulation and implementation of outer island and rural development programmes in collaboration with local communities, taking particular note of the needs of different groups, including, women, men, youth, disabled, those in isolated areas etc.",""]],"23":[[1,"74","2","Expand Access to Infrastructure and Technology","TSDFII Pillar 4 Organisational Outcomes require supporting government outputs to place greater focus on ensuring that infrastructure and technology is made more widely available to all groups throughout the Kingdom, within the constraints of cost and size.",""],[1,"100","5","National Infrastructure Investment Plan Implementation","Appropriate, well planned and maintained infrastructure that improves the everyday lives of the people and lowers the cost of business, by the adequate funding and implementation of the National Infrastructure Investment Plan (NIIP).",""],[1,"101","9","National Infrastructure Investment Plan Implementation","Appropriate, well planned and maintained infrastructure that improves the everyday lives of the people and lowers the cost of business, by the adequate funding and implementation of the National Infrastructure Investment Plan (NIIP).",""],[1,"102","22","National Infrastructure Investment Plan Implementation","Appropriate, well planned and maintained infrastructure that improves the everyday lives of the people and lowers the cost of business, by the adequate funding and implementation of the National Infrastructure Investment Plan (NIIP).",""],[1,"109","12","Support for Small-Scale Infrastructure and Appropriate Technology","increasing new opportunities for smaller scale infrastructure and technology more suited to our local conditions",""],[1,"116","5","Infrastructure Financing Mobilization","seek a range of funding opportunities from aid grants, appropriate borrowing, and joint public/private partnerships for important infrastructure requirements",""],[1,"120","12","Development of Financial, Communications, and Transport Services","facilitate the development of financial, communications and transport services which facilitate exchange between these two groups",""],[1,"124","10","Inclusive Infrastructure Planning","help all infrastructure development to take particular account of the needs of different sectors, and different groups (in particular, women, disabled, isolated etc.)",""]],"24":[[1,"75","3","Safe and Resilient Construction Technology and Retrofitting Programme","Structures that make greater use of safe and appropriate construction technology will improve the services provided by those structures, help to lessen maintenance, save on energy usage, and increase resilience to disasters.",""],[1,"75","3","Updated Building Codes and Compliance Strengthening","Updated building codes, with stronger compliance and awareness, are also essential.",""],[1,"124","5","Building Code Enforcement and Disaster-Resilient Siting","maintain and enforce appropriate building codes, taking account of disaster mitigation including placing structures away from disaster-prone areas, including from flooding",""],[1,"124","7","Local Building Industry Development Support","facilitate and support the development of the local building industry to be better able to build and maintain these structures",""],[1,"124","8","Infrastructure Standards Compliance for Aid-Funded Construction","ensure that aid-funded constructions and other infrastructure, including for the Pacific Games, is consistent with these standards",""],[1,"124","9","Post-Games Use and Maintenance of Pacific Games Facilities","seek options to ensure the continued use of the Pacific Games facilities after the games to help with operations and maintenance of these facilities so that they bring benefits for many years.",""]],"25":[[1,"20","10","Improved Land Use Planning and Enforcement","Improved land use planning, management and administration with stronger and appropriate enforcement which ensures the better provision of public spaces as well as private spaces, ensures more appropriate placement of infrastructure, better protects the environment, and limits risk, so as to improve safety conditions both for communities and business, working in harmony with a better application of the traditional land management system.",""],[1,"77","2","Land Use Planning and Enforcement Strengthening","Improved land use planning, management and administration with stronger and appropriate enforcement",""],[1,"89","1","Mandatory Environmental Impact Assessment for Major Development Projects","Subject all major development projects to a formal EIA",""],[1,"116","12","Legal and Regulatory Framework Strengthening","ensure the appropriate level of laws and regulation are in place, to facilitate law and order, protect consumer rights, promote honest business and market access,",""],[1,"118","11","Cultural Impact Review for International Agreements","ensure that before signing international agreements that careful consideration is given to the consequences of such agreement on our cultural values",""],[1,"124","13","Collaborative Land Governance and Enforcement Initiative","collaborative engagement among key stakeholders to ensure proper enforcement of existing Acts and policies, including wider access to land services as intended in the original design of the Tongan land system, taking particular note of the needs of women",""],[1,"124","14","Lease System Strengthening for Land Access and Collateral Use","strengthen the lease system to ensure better use of limited land and facilitate the use of land as collateral for",""],[1,"125","3","Land Tenure and Land Access Facilitation","promote and facilitate the realisation of land tenure and access to land",""],[1,"125","4","Informed Land Use Planning Awareness and Coordination","develop better understanding between government, land title holders, and the wider public of the importance of informed land use planning",""],[1,"125","5","Community and Business Participation in Public Space Development and Maintenance","encourage greater community and business participation in the development and maintenance of appropriate public spaces to complement the development of private spaces.",""],[1,"125","6","Implementation of Royal Land Commission Recommendations","consider the implementation of the Royal Land Commission (2011) recommendations.",""]],"26":[[1,"121","11","Police Professionalization and Community Policing Reform","improve the professionalism of the Police, with stronger community policing across the Kingdom, and application of appropriate technology, taking particular note of the needs of different groups, in particular women, disabled and others",""],[1,"121","12","Integrated Prison Management and Reintegration Approach","seek an appropriate balance between prison and other forms of punishment, as part of an integrated approach to improved management of prisoners and their reintegration into society",""],[1,"123","2","International Peacekeeping Cooperation and Skills Support","further build on cooperation with armed services in other partner countries to support international peacekeeping and the building of skills, including the support for communities that is provided by visiting defence staff",""],[1,"123","4","Regional Border Security and International Policing Cooperation","ensure active engagement with regional efforts to improve border security, international policing and other collaboration for improved international law and order.",""]],"27":[[1,"123","1","Regional and International Cooperation Support","continue to be a reliable and responsible member of the international community supporting the development of the Pacific region, including the Forum Secretariat and other regional and international bodies",""]],"28":[[1,"118","13","Cultural Heritage Storage and Display Capacity Development","develop an appropriate capacity to store and display items of historical and relevant cultural value",""],[1,"118","14","International Museum Linkages and Exhibition Exchange","encourage links with overseas museums with the view to having exhibitions of relevant cultural value here in Tonga",""]],"29":[[1,"36","3","Review of Ongoing Budget Support Viability","fiscal prudence will include careful consideration of the viability of ongoing budget support over the period of TSDF II",""],[1,"36","3","Government Revenue Mobilization for TSDF Implementation","The capacity to generate sufficient government revenues to fund the services required to implement the TSDF will be a major area of focus during the period of TSDF II",""],[1,"100","14","Macroeconomic Environment and Fiscal Management Improvement","Improving the macro- economic environment and fiscal management, including effective revenue services to ensure a level playing field and those services to the people can be appropriately funded.",""],[1,"102","8","Macro-Economic Environment and Fiscal Management Improvement","Improving the macro-economic environment and fiscal management, including effective revenue services to ensure a level playing field and those services to the people can be appropriately funded.",""],[1,"116","6","Tax Reform and Modernization Program","continue implementing tax reform and modernization programs to enhance revenue services and taxpayer compliance while encouraging investment",""],[1,"116","7","Domestic Credit and Foreign Exchange Reserve Management","manage domestic credit creation and foreign exchange reserves to ensure the convertibility of the pa'anga.",""]]}});